File Index

/crontab-root
Purpose: This crontab entry automates nginx log rotation every 15 minutes using logrotate utility.

/edge-subdomains.conf
Purpose: Configures nginx routing and proxy settings for multiple subdomains and services. Phase F: added a kingdom-tactics.shatteredarchive.dev server block (single subdomain for BOTH kingdom-tactics-client and -server — /api/kt/, /ws/kt (WebSocket upgrade), and /health proxy to the server; everything else to the client), mirroring the build.shatteredarchive.dev/auth.shatteredarchive.dev pattern, not a separate client/server subdomain pair. Live-verified via Host-header-override curl/http.request calls (no browser available in this environment) through the real recreated nginx container — every other subdomain regression-checked in the same pass. Scrum Poker (2026-07-28): added a scrum-poker.shatteredarchive.dev block on the same single-subdomain, resolver+variable pattern — /api/scrum/, /ws/scrum (WebSocket, proxy_read_timeout 3600 for long quiet stretches between stories) and /health to scrum-poker-server:63000, everything else to the SPA. Verified by running the REAL extracted block in a throwaway nginx container with the real images network-aliased as scrum-poker-server/-client: nginx -t clean, and all four routes plus a 101 upgrade exercised end-to-end without touching the live stack. 2026-07-29: added an ACTIVE real_ip block at the top — set_real_ip_from ${FRONT_PROXY_CIDR} / real_ip_header X-Forwarded-For / real_ip_recursive on. Load-bearing for the limit_* zones: they key on $binary_remote_addr, which behind the front proxy (DSL/nginx/shattered_archive.site) is that proxy's single address for ALL internet traffic, silently turning the per-IP limits into GLOBAL ones (10 room creations/min for the whole world, 128 total websockets — two teams would knock each other offline). FRONT_PROXY_CIDR is a REQUIRED env var supplied by the nginx service in BOTH compose files as "${FRONT_PROXY_CIDR:-144.217.6.225/32}" and substituted by the entrypoint's envsubst pass, same mechanism as ${NGINX_TLS_INCLUDE_FILE} — if it is ever unset, envsubst leaves the literal ${...} behind and nginx REFUSES TO START, so override it via env, never by editing this file. Must stay a /32 of the proxy itself: anything trusted here can forge X-Forwarded-For and skip the limits. Inert on the experimental stack (nothing reaches it via the front proxy). Verified in-container: rewrite fires only for a trusted source, and a forged XFF prefix still resolves to the real appended client because the front proxy appends and recursive walks right-to-left.

/edge.conf
Purpose: This file configures nginx to route HTTPS traffic to different upstream services based on the hostname.

/entrypoint.sh
Purpose: This script initializes NGINX server with self-signed TLS certificates and configures log rotation for the development environment.

/game-client.conf
Purpose: This file configures the Nginx server settings for the game client web application.

/kingdom-tactics-client.conf
Purpose: Phase F — per-container nginx conf baked into the kingdom-tactics-client image (SPA static serve, try_files fallback to index.html). Identical shape to mud-builder-client.conf; the edge subdomain routing lives in edge-subdomains.conf, not here.

/logrotate-nginx.conf
Purpose: Configures daily rotation and compression of nginx log files with 14-day retention.

/scrum-poker-client.conf
Purpose: Per-container nginx conf baked into the scrum-poker-client image (SPA static serve, try_files fallback to index.html). Same shape as mud-builder-client.conf, but the fallback is load-bearing here rather than incidental: room URLs are real paths (/room/3f2504e0-4f89-41d3-9a0c-0305e82c3301) meant to be pasted into chat and opened cold, so a direct hit must serve index.html rather than 404.

/shatteredarchive-dev-stub.conf
Purpose: This configuration file sets up nginx server settings for the shatteredarchive-dev development environment.

/ssl-params.conf
Purpose: Configures SSL parameters and security headers for local development with self-signed certificates.

/web-client.conf
Purpose: This file configures the Nginx web server for the client-side application.
